            {
                "entry_id": "751fcaf8-66ea-3a88-a0ca-54b3204a6c29",
                "word": "pommy",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "383078c9-6862-4708-b1ad-fba613d702c6",
                        "entry_id": "751fcaf8-66ea-3a88-a0ca-54b3204a6c29",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "pommies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1a393700-48b0-3641-ab4f-4f7bbd25e482",
                        "entry_id": "751fcaf8-66ea-3a88-a0ca-54b3204a6c29",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A pom; a person of British descent, a Briton; an Englishman."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Australia",
                            "New-Zealand",
                            "South-Africa",
                            "derogatory",
                            "often"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cff2a808-4cde-4e7d-b735-086a565e517b",
                                "sense_id": "1a393700-48b0-3641-ab4f-4f7bbd25e482",
                                "text": "Though Sir Oswald had taken on enough London veneer to be sneered at as a pommy in certain Australian circles, he had never acquired the high-class Englishman′s apparent equanimity or indifference before the prospect of cuckolding."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0e77cbe0-26a3-4851-91d3-32892aabd7d5",
                                "sense_id": "1a393700-48b0-3641-ab4f-4f7bbd25e482",
                                "text": "Rhona nodded her agreement. ‘That′s a very interesting answer from a new Aussie – and a Pommy into the bargain,’ she added."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "62e46a65-8dd9-4b47-b2dc-488d551b781f",
                                "sense_id": "1a393700-48b0-3641-ab4f-4f7bbd25e482",
                                "text": "During one of these acts of bravery by the English pilots I saw a great big tough Aussie with tears of frustration streaming down his face. He was shouting, ‘You magnificent, stupid Pommy bastard!’"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
